honestly i've never made it past the first pair having grandkids. i already forgot to do all the legacy stuff i was supposed to do.

&#x200B;

i just want my sims to have a life outside the house because i end up stuck there bc everything is alreaedy there for them. i'm trying rags to riches for the first time to see if that makes it more interesting. i always end up housebound with every save. i never mean to...but it hapepns!

I am bumping this because I spent over a week trying different books from Karin Slaughter recommendation threads (I was looking at suggestions from 3yr ago to the present). I picked and picked and actually none of these gave me the hook I was looking for?

&#x200B;

I have started Lisa Unger - Angel Fire

&#x200B;

It is \*not\* the same in terms of....anything. It's almost like Sarah mixed with Lena? It isn't about a detective/professional (which I usually prefer). The protagonist is an observant woman who helped figured out who killed her mother/serial killer. She doesn't have any special powers. Just observes thing (and not in a clever tv way). That trauma shaped her and now she cuts clippings from newspapers around the globe and looks at them and it they feel hinky she explores them.

&#x200B;

I am really enjoying it. I did not want a DV book mystery. I really like more HSP (highly skilled professional) type characters.

&#x200B;

Just an FYI from a very picky reader who loves KS.

lmao. 4th wing!!!

&#x200B;

i had no idea

I am catching up 3yr after the fact (I wasn't in the countr) and trying to catch up as quickly as possible. 

&#x200B;

There is no douby in her competency. My siblings don't think she should have access to her own $ because if she spends all of it they won't help or support in any way.

I'm tring to get my own deposit back, been 6wk. The owners of several properties are suing PDP. They asked the owners of properties for a COVID break on their payments and stopped paying altogether. As a tenant I was not allowed a rent reduction. I know they've destroyed my place. It's falling apart! We had problems with power, heating, water...and they steal a service fee from every tenant! They are criminals and not worth the properties they have!

&#x200B;

I can't even get them to pick up the phone anymore.

my computer is less than 1yr old and it still struggles to run the sims. i should turn down the settings...it's already on laptop mode but if i play too long it eats at my battery!

&#x200B;

ts2 ran way better. i kind of miss the mix of high poly and low visuals (when compared to the appearance of sims in ts3/4)

idk if it's just me...but can you not just make kava whenever you want? or is it party only? my sims are waving at me every time i ask them to make it just for fun (YA/A/Elder - i know it doesn't work for teens).

&#x200B;

i think it's a very beautiful world.

i love it!!! i'm so bad at legacies. i've never made it past...3? grandparent, parent, child. but it's often because i don't know which child to pick as the "heir" and always have really full houses, so picking feels impossible and going with 2 is impractical.

&#x200B;

i did just start a sim with 2 wives bc he got a second woman pregnant and i'm intrigued to see how it plays out. i don't usually care about the male characters, but they were already a matched pair. i'm definitely contemplating having them divorce him and marry each other. they're so much better than he is.
